# Atticus — environment template
#
#   cp ops/.env.example ops/.env    then fill in ops/.env
#
# ops/.env is gitignored. This file is committed and must never contain
# a real secret.
#
# TWO HOSTS. Deploy the same file to both; each reads only its own
# section plus SHARED. Nothing breaks if a host sees the other's vars,
# but the Plaud token path should exist only on WarDog.
#
#   WarDog  ingest    Plaud Cloud → GitHub        always-on
#   Forge   processor GitHub → transcribe/execute → GitHub
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE ON PLAUD AUTH: the official Plaud CLI is PAYWALLED and unused —
# see ADR-002. No password lives here either. The ingest transport is
# still undecided (SPEC §2.2.1: direct BLE / Android bridge / web
# fetcher), so the WarDog section below is provisional.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ══ SHARED — both hosts ══════════════════════════════════════════════

# Absolute path to the atticus-vault checkout on THIS host.
# Each host has its own clone; the paths need not match.
ATTICUS_VAULT_PATH=/srv/atticus/atticus-vault

# Git identity for automated commits. Distinguish the hosts so the vault
# history shows which side of the pipeline made each commit.
#   WarDog → "Atticus Ingest"
#   Forge  → "Atticus Processor"
ATTICUS_GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=Atticus
ATTICUS_GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=atticus@localhost

# Both hosts push to the same repo. Bounded retry on rebase conflict
# before quarantining and notifying. See SPEC §4.3.
ATTICUS_PUSH_RETRIES=3

# Failure notifications (SPEC T-70). Leave blank to disable.
# ntfy topic URL, or any endpoint accepting a POST body.
ATTICUS_NOTIFY_URL=

# DEBUG | INFO | WARNING | ERROR
ATTICUS_LOG_LEVEL=INFO


# ══ WARDOG — ingest only ═════════════════════════════════════════════

# PROVISIONAL — the ingest transport is undecided (SPEC §2.2.1).
# Whichever wins, the credential lives on WarDog and never touches Forge.

# Web-fetcher path: seeded Playwright session directory.
PLAUD_SESSION_ROOT=/home/atticus/.local/share/claude-fetchers/sessions

# Lookback window for the recording list. The seen.jsonl ledger handles
# dedupe, so overlap is free.
PLAUD_POLL_DAYS=2

# Direct-BLE path (SPEC option 1): the pin's Bluetooth address, once known.
# PLAUD_BLE_ADDRESS=


# ══ FORGE — processing only ══════════════════════════════════════════

# ── transcription ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same endpoint and model as the machine's existing dictation (hyprwhspr),
# deliberately: one transcription stack, not two. The API key is NOT here —
# it is read from ~/.config/ai/env at runtime.
ATTICUS_STT_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/audio/transcriptions
# gpt-4o-transcribe ($0.006/min) not gpt-4o-mini-transcribe ($0.003/min).
# Different job from dictation: nobody is waiting on this, so latency is free
# and accuracy is worth buying. A misheard word here silently becomes an
# autonomous agent's instruction — in dictation you'd see and fix it.
# ~$11/yr difference at 20 recordings/day.
ATTICUS_STT_MODEL=gpt-4o-transcribe
ATTICUS_STT_TIMEOUT=60

# Steering prompt. Measurably improves punctuation and capitalization —
# carried over from hyprwhspr's config and extended for instruction-shaped
# audio. Change with care.
ATTICUS_STT_PROMPT=Transcribe with proper capitalization, including sentence beginnings, proper nouns, titles, and standard English capitalization rules. The speaker is dictating a short instruction or request.

# ── the sanity gate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The transcript becomes the agent's prompt, so garbage in means an agent
# acting on garbage.

# Refuse to execute transcripts shorter than this.
ATTICUS_MIN_WORDS=3

# Optional wake phrase. Empty = execute every transcript that passes the
# word count. Set it (e.g. "atticus") and only transcripts starting with it
# are executed — everything else is filed as an unexecuted note.
#
# STRONGLY recommended for a wearable: without it, an overheard meeting or
# phone call becomes an instruction to an autonomous agent.
ATTICUS_WAKE_PHRASE=atticus

# ── execution ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave model unset to use the Claude Code default.
ATTICUS_CLAUDE_BIN=claude
ATTICUS_CLAUDE_MODEL=
ATTICUS_EXEC_TIMEOUT=1800
ATTICUS_SKILLS_DIR=

# Warn if a recording sits in inbox/ unprocessed longer than this.
# The queue's benefit — Forge may be offline, work waits — is also its
# failure mode: a dead Forge looks exactly like an idle one. See T-74.
ATTICUS_BACKLOG_ALARM_MINUTES=60


# ══ W8 — Plaud Embedded, CONTINGENT ══════════════════════════════════
#
# From the Plaud Developer Portal. NOT read by v1 — the iOS app is
# contingent and unbuilt (see ADR-001). Parked here so the credentials
# have one home rather than three. Belongs on WarDog if it ever fires,
# since W8's upload endpoint lands there too (T-84).
#
# Uncomment only when W8 actually triggers.

# PLAUD_EMBEDDED_CLIENT_ID=
# PLAUD_EMBEDDED_CLIENT_SECRET=
# PLAUD_EMBEDDED_API_KEY=
# PLAUD_EMBEDDED_API_HOST=


# ══ Not configured here ══════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Claude Code auth — the processor shells out to `claude -p`, which uses
# its own credential store on Forge. Do not duplicate an API key here.
#
# GitHub auth — one deploy key per host in ~/.ssh, not here. Two keys,
# both with write access to atticus-vault, independently revocable.
